course: dictionary
lesson: 4068
title: Geographic and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Geographic is a long word, but the sentence around it gives clues. «A compass points to magnetic north, which is not exactly the same place as the geographic North Pole.» Two places are set side by side here, so geographic must mean the true position on Earth, not the spot a compass points to.
explain: Geographic means to do with geography, the study of places, land, seas, countries and people. It also means to do with where things are on Earth. Geographic features are things like mountains, rivers and coasts, and a geographic map shows them.
explain: Geographic is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a geographic location. Geographical means the same thing, so you can use either word. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does «the true position on Earth» still make sense? If yes, you have it.
fact: Geographic means to do with geography, or to do with where things are on Earth.
fact: Geographic and geographical are both adjectives and mean the same thing.
fact: «Geographic features» are things like mountains, rivers and coasts.
fact: «The geographic North Pole» is the true North Pole on Earth, and it is in a different place from the magnetic north a compass points to.
fact: «The magnetic north pole» slowly moves every year, so the two north poles are not in the same place.
exercise: «A compass points to magnetic north, which is not exactly the same place as the geographic North Pole.» What does geographic mean here? | *The true position on Earth, as opposed to where a compass points | Very hot and dry | To do with music and singing
exercise: Which of these is a geographic feature? | A pencil case | *A mountain | A sentence about a dog | A birthday cake
exercise: Ruby says a geographic map shows where things are on Earth. What kinds of things does it show? | *Mountains, rivers and coasts | Next week's weather only | Recipes for dinner | Only the names of her friends
test: «In geography lessons, we study geographic features.» What does geographic tell us about these features? | They are always invisible | *They belong to geography, the study of places and land | They belong to music lessons
test: Which phrase is about where things are on Earth? | *The geographic location of the village | A loud drum beat | A soft pillow | A hot summer picnic
exam: Which sentence uses geographic correctly? | Geographic is a type of sandwich | The dog barked at the geographic cat | I geographic my lunch every day | *The geographic location of the village is near the river
